## What affects the cost of a Cardiff website?

- **How many pages you need.** A one-page site is a very different job from a site with a separate page for every service and area you cover.
- **What the site has to do.** Online payments, bookings, application forms or links to other systems all add work.
- **Built around you, or a template.** Designing around your business takes longer than dropping your logo into a theme, but it means the site is yours rather than looking like everyone else's.
- **Whether SEO is built in.** Some designers include on-page SEO as standard; others don't touch it. Always ask.
- **Who's doing the work.** With a larger agency you're also paying for account managers and project managers. If you work directly with the people building your site, you're mostly paying for the build.
- **What happens after launch.** Hosting, updates, backups and support are ongoing costs, and they're not always in the headline price.

## What you get at each level

**A one-page website, from £199.** A single, focused page covering who you are, what you do, where you work and how to get in touch. It suits a business with one main service that mainly needs to look credible and be easy to contact. You own the website, and it can grow into a multi-page site later without starting again.

**A multi-page service website, from £600.** A homepage plus separate pages for each main service, the areas you cover, your work and how to get in touch. This is usually the right choice if you offer several services or want work in several parts of Cardiff and the Vale, because each page can focus on one thing people actually search for. A five-page site and a fifteen-page site are different jobs, so the final price depends on how many pages and features you need.

**An online shop, from £800.** Selling online adds product pages, payments, delivery options and stock management. The final price depends on the platform, the number of products and categories, any bespoke features such as bookings or subscriptions, and whether you'd like us to upload your catalogue.

**A complex or bespoke build.** Custom integrations, member areas, large catalogues or multi-site set-ups are scoped individually. Check that every extra feature is something you'll actually use.

**Branding.** If you're starting from scratch, a logo and brand identity starts from £200 and can be designed alongside the website so everything matches from day one.

## Pay monthly in Cardiff: what £20 a month gets you

If a one-off bill isn't practical, a pay-monthly website spreads the cost. Here's exactly how ours works, including the three things you should check with any pay-monthly provider.

**What's included on every tier:** a professionally built, mobile-responsive website, your own custom domain, fast hosting with SSL, daily backups, contact and enquiry forms, Google Maps integration, Google Analytics setup, social media links, a testimonials section, case studies, small content changes (a new price, a new photo, updated opening hours), ongoing technical management and SEO foundations on every page. The tiers differ in how many new pages we add each month:

- **Starter:** £20 a month, 5 new pages a month
- **Growth:** £35 a month, 10 new pages a month
- **Scale:** £50 a month, unlimited new pages

Most pay-monthly sites are live within 5–7 days of us receiving your content and details. Google Business Profile setup is available as a £50 one-off add-on.

**1. Contract length.** There's a minimum 6-month term. After that it rolls monthly, and you can cancel with 30 days' notice.

**2. Design limits.** A pay-monthly site is built and managed by us, so changes are made on request rather than by you logging in. It isn't the right choice if you want to edit content yourself day to day, run an online shop or need a fully bespoke design. For those, a one-off build is better, and you can upgrade later with your domain and hosting moved across.

**3. Ownership.** With a pay-monthly website you don't own the website itself. Your domain is registered in your name, though, and if you leave you keep your domain and your text and photos.

### Pay monthly or one-off?

| | Pay-monthly website | One-off build |
|---|---|---|
| Upfront cost | None | Yes (one-page from £199) |
| Minimum term | 6 months, then 30 days' notice | None for the build |
| Domain and hosting | Included | Hosting £25 a month or £250 a year |
| Who edits the content | We do, on request | You do, with training |
| Who owns the website | We do. Your domain is in your name, and you keep your text and photos if you leave | You do |
| Best for | Getting online quickly with no technical work | Owning and managing your own site, shops and bespoke needs |

## What a website costs to run

The build is only part of the cost. Whichever route you choose, budget for:

**Hosting and your domain.** Pay-monthly sites include both. For a website you own, our UK hosting with SSL, Cloudflare CDN and daily backups is £25 a month or £250 a year.

**Maintenance.** WordPress, themes and plugins need regular updates. Outdated plugins and themes are the most common cause of hacked websites. Our maintenance plans roll monthly:

| Plan | Price | What it adds |
|---|---|---|
| Essential | £50 a month | Weekly core, theme and plugin updates · security scans and vulnerability monitoring · daily cloud backups with one-click restore · uptime and link monitoring · monthly performance and security report · 30 minutes' support |
| Growth | £75 a month | Everything in Essential · monthly basic SEO and performance checks with speed optimisation · priority support · 1 page plus 1 case study or blog post a month · 1 hour's support |
| Pro | £99 a month | Everything in Essential and Growth · monthly advanced SEO health check · 2 new pages and 2 blog posts or case studies a month · 1.5 hours' support |

Cheaper maintenance plans exist. When you compare them, check whether updates are weekly or "as needed", whether backups can be restored quickly, and whether any support time or new content is included.

**SEO.** Every site we build has on-page SEO foundations. If you want to compete for busier Cardiff searches, our [local SEO for Cardiff businesses](/seo-cardiff/) starts from £200 a month.

## How long does it take?

Most of our website projects are finished within 7–14 days, depending on the size of the job and how quickly we receive your content. Pay-monthly sites are usually live within 5–7 days of us getting your content. The biggest cause of delays is waiting for text and photos, so gathering them early saves time.

