## Don't just compare the headline price

The cheapest quote isn't always the best value. A site that can't be found on Google, doesn't turn visitors into enquiries, or needs rebuilding in a couple of years costs more in the end. The budget should change the *scope* of a website (fewer pages, fewer features), not the foundations. Even a one-page site should load quickly on a phone, say clearly what you do and where, and make it easy to get in touch.

When you compare quotes, get three things in writing: a fixed price, a list of what's included, and what the site will cost each year after launch.

## Cardiff website cost FAQs

**Is a £199 website any good?**

It can be, if it's the right size for your business. Ours is a single, properly built WordPress page with on-page SEO foundations, built mobile-first, and you own it. It isn't meant to replace a multi-page site for a business covering lots of services and areas.

**What's the cheapest way to get a professional website in Cardiff?**

If you'd rather not pay upfront, a pay-monthly website from £20 a month includes the domain, hosting and management, with a 6-month minimum term. If you'd rather own it outright, a one-page site from £199 is the lowest one-off cost.

**Do I own a pay-monthly website?**

No. The website stays ours, but your domain is registered in your name, and if you leave you keep your domain and your text and photos. If you want to own the website itself, choose a one-off build.

**What will I pay each year after launch?**

That depends on what you need. A pay-monthly site bundles hosting and management into the monthly fee. A website you own needs hosting (£25 a month or £250 a year) and, ideally, a maintenance plan from £50 a month. All our prices include VAT.

